From 06a1b52e6b55699c36a1fa7a04a87ef6901764cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Junod <donujp@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 19:44:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/11] tests/color: Exercise shutdown at asynchronous delivery
 boundaries

Add a color-lifecycle test that uses the delivery hook to park each
asynchronous step, tear down the color manager, store, device or
profile involved, and then deliver the parked result: colord connection
at startup (queued success and cancelled startup), every step of device
profile generation (directory query and creation, profile write,
generation result, EFI panel color info with and without fallback), a
caller that cancels a shared request, profiles assigned from colord,
ICC directory queries and reads, locally generated profiles becoming
ready around shutdown and finalization, and profiles created or kept
alive after the store is finalized. Each case checks that callbacks
complete without touching freed objects, that cancelled requests report
cancellation, and that the objects are finalized.

Each case runs as its own invocation. Teardown destroys the test
context exactly once.

Link: TBD-MR
